window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Elandra Strome is a grief counselor who can’t heal her own heart. Six months after her sister’s death, she drifts through life like a shadow—numb, detached, and colorless. But when a cryptic message leads her to an abandoned greenhouse hidden in a forgotten corner of the city, Elandra stumbles into a place where the veil between worlds grows thin—and where grief becomes a gateway to the extraordinary.</p> <p>Inside this surreal gallery, she meets Cael, a stranger with impossible knowledge of her pain—and an otherworldly presence that stirs something long dormant within her. As their connection deepens, Elandra is drawn into a metaphysical journey that blurs the lines between memory and destiny, dreams and desire, soul and cosmos.</p> <p>To uncover the truth of her soul’s purpose—and to rekindle the bond with the one she lost—Elandra must awaken parts of herself she thought were gone forever. But opening the heart comes with its own risks, especially when it bridges realms not meant to touch.</p> <p>Luminous and emotionally resonant, <i>The Mirror Between Worlds</i> is a visionary novel of loss, awakening, and a love that transcends time and reality.</p>"; 
